<h2 id='what-is-docparser'>🗂️ What Is Docparser?</h2>

<p>Docparser is a cloud-based document data extraction platform that converts PDFs, scanned files, and Word documents into structured, actionable data. You configure "parsers" — essentially rule sets — that tell the system exactly which fields to pull from a document type. Those extracted fields then flow into spreadsheets, CRMs, property management systems, or workflow tools via native integrations or Zapier.</p>

<p>For property management specifically, that means you can point Docparser at an incoming lease PDF and automatically extract tenant name, unit number, lease start and end dates, monthly rent, security deposit amount, and any custom clauses you care about — without a single manual keystroke after initial setup. The same logic applies to <a href='https://realestateopshub.com/guides/listing-document-workflows'>listing intake sheets</a>, maintenance vendor invoices, and insurance certificates.</p>

<p>Docparser is not a property management system itself. It sits upstream of your PM stack as a data capture layer, feeding clean structured data into whatever tools you already use.</p>

